---
id: org.dxos.index-core
name: IndexCore
version: 0.1.0
---

`@dxos/index-core` is the ECHO indexer: `IndexEngine` reads entities from data sources (Automerge
documents, feed blocks), writes them to SQLite indexes (objectSnapshot, reverseRef, fts, activity)
and advances one cursor per source. Two hosts run it: `EchoHost` on a device, and EDGE's Indexer
Durable Object in db-service.

The indexer is also the one component that reads every object of a space. So it records **indexer
intents**: durable follow-up work that another component must do because of something the indexer
saw. An intent commits in the transaction that writes the index rows, so it commits no later than
the cursor that passes the object, and a crash cannot lose it. This spec defines the intent
mechanism, its two kinds — convergence-key (existing) and feed-options (new) — and how the indexer
treats a feed's indexing and retention options. The store side of those options is in
`org.dxos.feed`; the `Feed` object fields are in
`org.dxos.echo` [F-7].

```diagram
diagram flow=down
group echo "ECHO object" {
  node FeedObj "Feed object" ref="packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts"
}
group index "@dxos/index-core" below echo {
  node Engine "IndexEngine" ref="packages/core/echo/index-core/src/index-engine.ts"
  node Intents "FeedOptionsIntents" right-of Engine ref="packages/core/echo/index-core/src/feed-options-intent-store.ts"
}
group hosts "Store hosts" below index {
  node Host "EchoHost" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/db-host/echo-host.ts"
  node Indexer "Indexer DO"
  node Space "FeedSpace DO"
  node Store "FeedStore" ref="packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts"
  node Source "FeedDataSource" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/db-host/feed-data-source.ts"
}
edge Engine -> FeedObj "indexes"
edge Engine -> Intents "records"
edge Host -> Intents "takes"
edge Indexer -> Intents "takes"
edge Host -> Store "setFeedOptions"
edge Indexer -> Space "setFeedOptions"
edge Space -> Store
edge Source -> Store "reads options"
```

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.

| Term       | URI                         |
| ---------- | --------------------------- |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`     |
| `scenario` | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0` |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0` |
| `service`  | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`  |
| `table`    | `org.dxos.mdl.table@1.0`    |

## Concepts

```mdl
service FeedOptionsIntentStore
  desc: |
    The feed-options intent log in the index database, the
    sibling of ConvergenceKeyIntentStore. IndexEngine records into it; the host takes and clears through
    IndexEngine pass-throughs (takeFeedOptionsIntents, clearFeedOptionsIntents).
  ops:
    migrate() → void
    record(intents: FeedOptionsIntent[]) → void                       # inside the index-row transaction, replacing the feed's row [F-1.2]
    take() → { maxId: number; intents: FeedOptionsIntent[] }         # newest per (spaceId, feedId) [F-2.2]
    clear(spaceId: SpaceId, feedId: string, upToId: number) → void   # rows up to upToId only [F-1.3]
  note: |
    FeedOptionsIntent is { spaceId, feedId, namespace, indexing?: IndexingOptions, retention?: RetentionOptions }.
    IndexerIntent = ConvergenceKeyIntent | FeedOptionsIntent, tagged by `kind` [F-1.1].
```

```mdl
table feedOptionsIntents: One pending "apply this feed's options" intent.
  store: index database (feed_options_intent_migrations)
  columns:
    id: INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT   # monotonic; clear() is bounded by it
    spaceId: TEXT
    feedId: TEXT                            # the Feed object's entity id
    namespace: TEXT                         # data | trace
    options: TEXT                           # json { indexing?, retention? } as read from the object
  key: id
  indexes:
    - idx_feedOptionsIntents_feed(spaceId, feedId, id): take() picks the newest row per feed [F-2.2]
  new: table
```

```mdl
table convergenceKeyIntents: One pending "check this key's group for duplicates" intent.
  store: index database (convergence_key_intent_migrations)
  columns:
    id: INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT
    spaceId: TEXT
    convergenceKey: TEXT
  key: id
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Indexer intents

  desc: |
    An intent means "this may need doing; do it", not "this is needed", so servicing one twice is
    harmless and losing one is a bug.

  req F-1.1:
    when: an intent kind is defined
    then: it is a member of the IndexerIntent tagged union in @dxos/index-core, with its own table
          and migration set in the index database, and a record / take / clear store

  req F-1.2:
    when: IndexEngine derives intents from the objects of a batch
    then: it records them in the transaction that writes those objects' index rows

  req F-1.3:
    when: take() runs
    then: it returns the pending intents and the highest intent id it read; clear(…, upToId) removes
          only rows up to that id, so an intent recorded while the consumer works survives

  req F-1.4:
    when: a consumer fails, or the host stops before clear()
    then: the intents stay pending, and the next index pass — every host runs one at startup —
          offers them again

  req F-1.5:
    when: an object with a non-empty @meta.convergenceKey is indexed
    then: a convergence-key intent { spaceId, convergenceKey } is recorded, and EchoHost's
          ConvergenceKeyMerger services it after the Automerge leg of the pass
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Feed-options intent

  req F-2.1:
    when: IndexEngine indexes an object of type org.dxos.type.feed
    then: it records a feed-options intent { spaceId, feedId, namespace, indexing, retention };
          feedId is the Feed object's entity id and namespace defaults to data

  req F-2.2:
    when: several feed-options intents for one (spaceId, feedId) are pending
    then: take() returns only the newest per feed

  req F-2.3:
    when: an index pass finishes its object leg on a device
    then: EchoHost takes the pending feed-options intents, calls FeedStore.setFeedOptions for each,
          and clears each once its apply has committed

  req F-2.4:
    when: an index pass finishes its object leg on EDGE
    then: the Indexer DO takes the pending feed-options intents, calls setFeedOptions on the space's
          FeedSpace DO for each, and clears each once the call has returned

  req F-2.5:
    when: a feed's options change and its intent is not applied yet
    then: the feed is indexed and trimmed under its previous options; the store converges once the
          intent is applied
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Feeds with indexing disabled

  req F-3.1:
    when: FeedDataSource (EchoHost or EDGE) reads blocks of a feed whose stored options have
          indexing.enabled = false
    then: it skips them and still advances its cursor past them, so no index row is written for them

  req F-3.2:
    when: options that disable indexing are applied
    then: the feed's existing rows are removed from every index in the next index pass

  req F-3.3:
    when: a query answered from the index runs (Filter.text, a type query over the space)
    then: it returns no item of a feed with indexing disabled

  req F-3.4:
    when: Feed.query(feed) runs on a feed with indexing disabled
    then: it returns the feed's items: the host query executor reads that feed's blocks from the
          feed store and matches them in memory instead of reading the index

  req F-3.5:
    when: options that re-enable indexing are applied
    then: every block the feed still retains is indexed — EDGE resets that feed's own cursor;
          EchoHost, whose feed cursor is per (space, namespace), runs a one-off backfill cursor
          (`backfill/<namespace>/<feedId>`) that reads the feed to its end while the namespace
          cursor skips it, then is deleted

  req F-3.6:
    when: an item is appended on EDGE to a feed with indexing disabled
    then: FeedSpace still notifies the Indexer DO, so function triggers on the feed keep firing;
          only the index write is skipped
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Retention in the index

  req F-4.1:
    when: the feed store deletes blocks by retention
    then: their rows are removed from every index in the next index pass, so no query returns an
          item the store no longer holds; a row is removed only when the block it was last written
          from (objectMeta.queueInsertionId) was trimmed, so a live feed object whose newer block
          survives keeps its row

  req F-4.2:
    when: an index-answered query returns items of a feed with retention.maxAge
    then: items whose block timestamp is older than now - maxAge are left out, before any trim
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: An intent survives a crash before apply
  given: a Feed object whose retention changed and was indexed, so a feed-options intent is recorded
  when: the host stops before applying it, then starts again
  then:
    - the startup index pass applies the intent and clears it
    - take() returns no feed-options intent afterwards
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: A newer intent recorded during apply survives
  given: a feed-options intent with id 7 taken by the host
  when: the feed's options change again and intent 8 is recorded before clear(…, 7)
  then: after clear(…, 7), take() returns intent 8
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Disable and re-enable indexing
  given: a feed with 3 indexed items found by Filter.text('hello')
  when: Feed.setIndexing(feed, { enabled: false }) runs and an index pass completes
  then:
    - Filter.text('hello') returns none of the feed's items
    - Feed.query(feed) still returns all 3 items
    - after Feed.setIndexing(feed, { enabled: true }) and an index pass, Filter.text('hello') finds them again
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Trimmed items leave the index
  given: a feed with retention { maxLength: 5 } and 5 indexed items
  when: 1 item is appended and an index pass completes
  then: a text query for the oldest item returns nothing
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Indexing of a feed can be fully disabled.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: A feed's indexing and retention options, set on the Feed ECHO object, flow down to the feed store through a new kind of indexer intent.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Convergence-key and feed-options intents are two kinds of one IndexerIntent union, each in its own table with the same record / take / clear contract. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.3, F-1.4]
  why: The convergence-key contract already guarantees that an indexed change cannot be forgotten across a crash; separate tables leave its migrations untouched.
  rejected:
    - "One intents table with a kind column: it needs a data migration of the convergence-key table for no behavioural gain."
```

```mdl
decision D-4: The feed-options intent is recorded for every indexed Feed object, latest-wins per feed, and applied by whichever host owns the store — EchoHost directly, EDGE's Indexer DO through FeedSpace. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2]
  why: Both hosts run the same IndexEngine, so one producer serves both; only the current options matter, so older pending intents carry nothing.
  rejected:
    - "Have the feed store read the Feed object: EDGE's FeedSpace DO has no Automerge access."
    - "Send options with each FeedService call, as namespace is today: EDGE would never see a change made while no one appends."
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Disabling indexing skips the feed's blocks in FeedDataSource and purges its existing index rows; re-enabling backfills what the store still retains. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.5]
  why: FeedDataSource is where both hosts read feed blocks into the index; the device cursor is per namespace, so re-enabling needs its own backfill.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: A feed with indexing disabled is still readable through Feed.query, and its function triggers on EDGE keep firing. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.4, F-3.6]
  why: "Indexing" is read as the search index only; Feed.query reads the store, and triggers are a separate consumer of the same notification.
  rejected:
    - "Make a disabled feed unreadable except by cursor: it breaks every reader of trace and log feeds."
```

```mdl
decision D-7: Items deleted by retention are removed from every index. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.1]
  why: Today deleteOldestBlocks leaves index rows behind, so a query can return an item the store no longer has.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Feed-options intents are rows of a new `feedOptionsIntents` table, with the options as one JSON column and an index on (spaceId, feedId, id) for the newest-per-feed take. Fills in [D-3] and [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [feedOptionsIntents, FeedOptionsIntentStore, F-2.2]
  why: The row carries the options themselves, so the consumer needs no second read of the object; recording a row per indexing of a Feed object stays cheap because take() collapses them.
  rejected:
    - "Upsert one row per feed: a concurrent record during apply would overwrite the row that clear() is about to delete, losing the newer options."
```

```mdl
decision D-9: For a feed with indexing disabled, the host query executor reads the feed store and matches in memory, because Feed.query is answered from the index and would otherwise return nothing once the feed's rows are purged. Supersedes the FeedService.queryFeed wording of [D-6].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.4]
  supersedes: D-6
  why: Feed.query goes through Database.query with a feed scope, which the executor answers from objectMeta; reading the store keeps the item set without indexing it.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: An entity-meta row records the insertion id of the block it was last written from, and retention removes a row only when that block was trimmed; rows written before the column existed fall back to matching by position. Fills in [D-7].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.1]
  why: A live feed object re-appends whole under the same id, so deleting by object id would remove objects whose older versions were trimmed.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Applying an intent runs the index side first (purge on disable, backfill seed on re-enable) and is idempotent, so a crash before the intent is cleared is redone on retry; a failing intent stays pending and is retried on every pass. Fills in [D-4] and [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.4, F-2.3, F-3.2, F-3.5]
  why: The store's `changed` is false on a retry, so the index side cannot key off it.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Index-answered feed queries drop items older than maxAge, using objectMeta.updatedAt, which holds the block timestamp. Fills in [D-7].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.2]
  why: Reads must hide expired items before the lazy trim deletes them (org.dxos.feed [F-2.2]), and the index already stores the block time.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: record() deletes the feed's pending row before inserting the new one, so feedOptionsIntents holds at most one row per Feed object. Refines [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [feedOptionsIntents, FeedOptionsIntentStore, F-2.2]
  why: A row per indexing grows with the object's edit history while applies keep failing; the replacement row takes a new AUTOINCREMENT id, so the race D-8 rejected an upsert for cannot erase it.
```

